"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mysterious 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3807810236" "Tunnels Layout"
// DetailString :
"P1464426829" "You found what exactly this Longbow group was looking for; a layout of the tunnels system beneath Praetoria. Looking it over, you notice several areas circled with notes from someone, most likely Anti-Matter. The notes read:<br><br>'Good spot, no Resistance here.'<br><br>'Clean out ghouls here and move in'<br><br>The last spot circled is right beneath Keyes Island, though there is no comment next to it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LongbowData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4221502910" "Longbow Communication Device"
// DetailString :
"P463190660" "You acquired the communication device used by the Longbow Officer you defeated. This technology seems somewhat primitive compared to what you're used to, but you're able to tinker with it to find the last recording sent.<br><br>'We're moving through the tunnels now, but it's not going to be easy bringing down Tyrant and his Praetorians. We need to take the fight to the surface, even if it means working together with Arachnos. I don't know why they're here, but it looks like they want the same thing we do. We can worry about Recluse later, Tyrant is the <i>real</i> enemy in Praetoria.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArachnosData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3416713824" "The Arachnos Assault"
// DetailString :
"P2566835646" "You stopped Arachnos from teleporting away and were able to recover some data on their plans. Reading it over, you discover their leader's name is 'Lord Recluse' and is based out of the 'Rogue Isles'. Most of what is written here is not too interesting, mainly just schematics for old technology that Arachnos uses to arm their men. What catches your eye is something at the end, a note from an Operative:<br><br>'Recluse ordered us to do everything possible to bring Cole down and prevent him from getting over to here. Seems like he was real spooked from the last report Sands sent in. Word is Sands found out that here in Praetoria, Recluse <i>died</i> at the hands of Cole.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - OperativeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3638973673" "Arachnos Communication"
// DetailString :
"P697482704" "You defeated the Arachnos operative and found on him instructions from a man named 'Arbiter Sands'.<br><br>'Look, between this and the Faultline project, I'm real busy, real busy, real important. So let's just keep the whole usual, 'Hail Arachnos, hail Lord Recluse' aside, okay? You're going to get the bombs planted in that office, and those Destined Ones will get them set up in the tunnels. Blow them up, get it done, and then we'll all get some cofffee afterwards.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BombClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2380995605" "Arachnos Bomb"
// DetailString :
"P1332081743" "You destroyed the Arachnos bomb before it went off, though you found something disturbing on the remains of the device. Looking it over, it appears that there are three more of these bombs planted somewhere in Neutropolis!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KangClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1716483099" "Destined Ones"
// DetailString :
"P3589215154" "You received the following transmissions from Interrogator Kang:<br><br>'{HeroName}, I've found where the Destined Ones are hiding out. I'm sending you the location now and I'll meet you there. Also... I've been doing some investigating onto the origin of Arachnos and Longbow, where they come from, why they're here. I think I'm getting close to something that may be <i>very</i> big. When the time comes, I'd like to know if I can count on you to help me uncover this case. You don't need to answer now. I'll see you soon.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3618426183" "Calvin Scott's Plan"
// DetailString :
"P1771382583" "You received a long code to use on one of the computer's at the base of Anti-Matter's reactor. With this code, you'll be able to access information that is stored within the computer."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - AntiMatterArc1Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3861763672" "Anti-Matter's Thanks"
// tDetailString :
"P1560347761" "Anti-Matter isn't someone who thanks someone very often. He's known for being very difficult to work with and very irritable. However, you managed to actually get him to thank you after a series of events you call...<br><br><color gold>View from the Other Side</color><br><br>Anti-Matter requested your help in dealing with a situation that was placed on his shoulders: handling the continued problem of Arachnos and Longbow. Your first outing found you fighting off Longbow alongside Interrogator Kang, cleaning out one of Anti-Matter's labs. Longbow was there looking for something, but you weren't sure what exactly it was.<br><br>When you returned, Anti-Matter informed you he was put in charge of solely removing the Arachnos soldiers in Praetoria, something he was not too happy with. With Anti-Matter and Interrogator Kang's help, you stopped an Arachnos bombing plot in Neutropolis and apprehended three 'Destined Ones' working for Arachnos. Kang warned you, however, that he was investigating something very big and that he may possibly need your help in the future.<br><br>After the plot was foiled, Anti-Matter requested your help in investigating a strange disturbance in his lab. It was there you met a man named Dark Watcher, who asked that you try to forgive Longbow for their ignorance, saying that they only wish to do the right thing, much like yourself. This was a little difficult to handle, given that afterwards you were ambushed by a squad of Longbow.<br><br>You didn't have much time to rest after that. Anti-Matter informed you Arachnos has gained control of one of his reactors and were planning to blow it up. He was told to allow Arachnos to blow it up in order to show to the people how dangerous they were so that Anti-Matter's 'project' could be justified. Anti-Matter, however, was not one to allow one of his creations to be destroyed so simple. He requested that you stop Arachnos along with Interrogator Kang, given that any other group in Praetoria that <i>could</i> stop the attack was ordered not to.<br><br>You went against the main force of Arachnos and stopped their plot to blow up Anti-Matter's reactor, earning Anti-Matter's gratefulness, even though he surely was going to be punished for going against direct orders."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4039194290" "<color orange>Anti-Matter mumbles to himself.</color><br><br>Do you know how much work is put on my shoulders, {HeroName}. Too much. Cole thinks I'm like that <i>idiot</i> Berry, that I can just wave my hand and make something in a matter of moments. Well, I <i>can't</i>, but what I <i>can</i> do is make something that's <i>good</i>. Look around you at these reactors of mine. They're efficient, powerful, and will stand the test of time.<br><br>Now, look at Berry's work in his city. It's already beginning to crumble, and he's simply moving on to his 'next big thing'. He should be ashamed of his work, and yet, he gets all the glory. Is it right? Fair? It isn't. And further, it isn't fair that now <i>I'm</i> tasked to deal with these <i>otherworlders</i>. As if I didn't have enough to deal with. Cole claims Berry is 'busy', but I <i>highly</i> doubt that."
// AcceptString :
"P2305670824" "So... who are these 'other worlders'?"
// SendOffString :
"P1433280659" "<color orange>Anti-Matter lets out a long sigh.</color><br><br>They call themselves <color yellow>Longbow</color>. They just started spilling out of the tunnels one day, making a mess out of everything. They're some sort of spandex-wearing idealists, spouting about delivering 'justice' and giving the people 'freedom'. All I know is that they're causing me nothing but problems. A group of them have attacked one of my labs. I'd go handle it myself, but I've got ten other things that I'm tasked with doing, of course. It's not like one of <i>my</i> labs is important.<br><br>Some investigator or interrogator went down there before to look into it, think his name was <color yellow>Kang</color> or something. I don't need any PPD dying in my labs, that'll just be one more thing that will be held over my head. I need you to go in there and stabilize the situation, {HeroName}. I hear that's what you do best."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1979643002" "Kick Longbow out of Anti-Matter's Lab"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3806671846" "Look, I've got no time to go over things again. Take notes or something when I talk to you, I'm backlogged enough as it is."
// TaskTitle :
"P2814510131" "<color deepskyblue>View from the Other Side</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1450383955" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: The New Team</color>"

