// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2699364936" "I've heard all about the situation, {HeroName}. You deserve an explanation about why exactly we're working with Arachnos."
// Answer Text :
"P2562100399" "I'm listening."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2105806759" "Lord Recluse has promised the Resistance support in the form of weapons and technology. Now, previously, they were our only option. Of course, I know <i>why</i> Arachnos was so gung-ho about helping us. They found out that Cole killed the Praetorian version of Lord Recluse a very long time ago; don't ask me how, or even why Cole did such a thing.<br><br>However, we're now starting to receive some support from Longbow and a man called <color yellow>Dr. Sheridan</color> in the form of a <color yellow>Rift Chamber</color>. I can explain everything to you when the time comes.<br><br>But for now, if you're going to be saving that reactor, I'll need you to retrieve information that Anti-Matter is working on."
// Answer Text :
"P2328853816" "How am I going to do that?"
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P948399724" "Take this code. Dr. Sheridan says that you should be able to use it to hack into the computer.<br><br><color yellow>The computer should be somewhere at the base of the reactor.</color> You'll be able to find out what exactly Anti-Matter is working on, and we'll be able to gain some support from Longbow."
// Answer Text :
"P1881143145" "I'll see what I can do."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro1 Text :
"P2107194272" "<color orange>You put in the password Calvin Scott sent you and find the following information...</color><br><br>The reactor cores help power all of Nova Praetoria, but more importantly, they help to move forward the plans to build the <color yellow>War Walker</color>, incredible machines built by Anti-Matter to wipe out all enemies that stand in our way. Once they have served their primary purpose, they can be used to easily wipe out the Resistance problem.<br><br>The plans to reveal the War Walkers involves the full support of the people of Praetoria. Then, we shall use the beacon in Neuron's tower to begin the full assault."
// Answer Text :
"P1519779196" "(Take the information and leave)"
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P3778896468" "<color orange>The computer seems to require a long password that you do not have.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3278961712" "This is ridiculous! {HeroName}, this is... the nerve... of <i>everyone</i>! Arachnos troops have <i>taken over</i> one of my reactors! Some fool named <color yellow>Arbiter Sands</color> is leading their troops and plans to <i>blow up</i> one of my own creations! Do you have any idea, <i>any</i> idea how catastrophic that will be?! The other two reactors can survive the blast, I <i>designed</i> them to incase one collapsed. But none of Berry's makeshift toys will survive the impact. Of course, I <i>told</i> him to design them that way, but he wouldn't listen! <i>Half of Neutropolis would be wiped away if that reactor explodes!</i><br><br>Do you know who will be blamed for that? <i>I</i> will, at least by the people! But what am I ordered to do? No, not, 'drop everything and stop Arachnos'. No, I'm ordered to <i>work harder on my projects and allow it to happen.</i> The fools! They want to give us a good reason to <i>hate</i> Arachnos, a good reason for my project. But I never even wanted to fall from Praetorship just to work on this project. I never wanted <i>any</i> of this. And I don't want the destruction of one of <i>my</i> creations be what fuels this little war!<br><br>That's why I'm turning to <i>you</i>, {HeroName}. I can't stop this, but <i>you</i> can."
// AcceptString :
"P60296734" "I'm on it. We can get the rest of the PPD to help."
// SendOffString :
"P3229763316" "We can't, {HeroName}. The 'powers that be' have ensured the PPD won't be around to handle the situation. Well, all except one. I've gotten word that <color yellow>Interrogator Kang</color> is on the scene. But that one man doesn't have <i>your</i> abilities. He can't handle this on his own. You need to go down there and stop Arachnos from blowing up my reactors. They have an Arachnos flyer in here and actually <i>disabled</i> our sonic fencing defenses! <br><br><color orange>They're out there in full force. I'd bring any other Powers Division that you can, or at least go in prepared to fight the full force of Arachnos.</color>Take this device. It will reboot the sonic fencing defenses in the area to destroy the Arachnos flyer. I've been given orders to preserve it, but if worse comes to worse, I need you to blow that thing up.<br><br>You and Kang are the only people who can stop this, {HeroName}.<br><br><color Paragon>Resistance working undercover for Calvin Scott should call him now to discuss events with Anti-Matter.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P786577505" "Save Anti-Matter's Reactor and Neutropolis!"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2964682308" "{HeroName}, <i>you</i> don’t have the time to be talking to me right now!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P266253789" "<color deepskyblue>Part Five: Praetoria's Last, Best Hope</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P43794245" "Arachnos have fortified the area around Anti-Matter's reactor to ensure they have it under complete control. Little do they know that the order has been given to let it explode.<br><br>It's up to you know to protect the lives of every single citizen that lives in Neutropolis."
// Script Variable DisplayText :
"P874720767" "Arachnos to defeat"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3383608100" "Nothing"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3151704988" "<t=4 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>This is really getting annoying. How hard is it for a guy to blow up a reactor around here?<t=5 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3  d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>Get this flyer's weapons online, we're just going to do this the easy way!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P4222132512" "<t=4 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>Ugh, seriously?! Activating emergency teleporter...!"
// Script Variable HERO_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3020412258" "{HeroName}! Anti-Matter may be difficult to deal with, but I suppose it shouldn't be said that he doesn't care for the people of Praetoria.<em>When this is all over, you and I have some very important business to handle.<em>Until then, let's move forward and stop Arachnos!"
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3012451806" "I'm sorry... you need to save Neutropolis now!"
// Script Variable NPC_DIALOG_NAME :
"P4105117061" "Computer"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P4090536126" "Don't let any Praetorians through!"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P117897351" "FIRE!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P1908114411" "Today we serve the glory of Lord Recluse in Praetoria! We will show Cole his true might!"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P581008225" "Kill the Praetorians!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P4051937475" "They think Primal Earth is weak, that we will fall over and die, but they shall learn to fear Arachnos!"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P2321407976" "Fire everything! Take them down!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P1305570891" "We've made it this far, not even Cole can stop us now!"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P515246603" "You can't stop this, Powers Division! Arachnos' might will prevail!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P3036727606" "Today we make our stand. Today we will die for the glory of Lord Recluse!"
